cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MBESS, please cite the package together with the two articles listed under references."
type: software
title: "MBESS: The MBESS R Package"
authors:
  - family-names: Kelley
    given-names: Ken
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4756-8360"
    affiliation: "University of Notre Dame"
version: 5.0.1
date-released: "2026-06-04"
license:
  - GPL-2.0-only
  - GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/yelleKneK/MBESS"
repository-artifact: "https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=MBESS"
url: "https://kenkelley.org/r-packages/"
abstract: >-
  Implements methods that are useful in designing research studies and
  analyzing data, with particular emphasis on methods developed for or used
  within the behavioral, educational, and social sciences, broadly defined:
  effect sizes, confidence intervals for effect sizes (including standardized
  and noncentral effect sizes), sample size planning from the accuracy in
  parameter estimation, power analytic, equivalence, and minimum-risk point
  estimation perspectives, mediation analysis, properties of distributions,
  and utility functions. On CRAN since 2006 and fully supported; new
  methodological development now takes place in its successor package,
  DMAR, and the two are designed to coexist.
keywords:
  - R package
  - effect sizes
  - confidence intervals
  - noncentral distributions
  - sample size planning
  - accuracy in parameter estimation
  - power analysis
  - mediation analysis
  - reliability
